# Voxly standing rules

docs/SPEC.md is the source of truth. It wins over the design images in docs/reference/ and over every other document, comment, chat, or prompt. The images show general look and feel only. Where they disagree with docs/SPEC.md, follow the specification.

The stack is React 18, Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS 3.4 (pinned), and Supabase (Postgres, Auth, Storage, Realtime). The product is a PWA first. A Capacitor wrap comes later.

Enable row-level security on every table.

Never use or expose the Supabase service-role key. Never put secrets in any variable whose name starts with VITE_.

Users can never change their own role, status, verified flag, or badges. Reader is the default role. Writer is granted automatically on first publish. There is no moderator role and no admin role. The Founder account is only voxly369@gmail.com, and only when that email is confirmed. Only that Founder moderates or administers.

Use Inter for interface text. Use Fraunces for reading and writing text, screen titles, and the wordmark. The accent is coral #FF5A3C. The verified badge is purple #8B5CF6. Dark mode is the default.

Every image has a fallback and never shows a broken icon.

Loading, Error, and Empty states are mutually exclusive.

The product is in-app only. Do not add sharing to other platforms or downloads.

Do only what the current numbered prompt says. Features not in the current prompt stay scheduled for later. Report any command you skipped. Never delete, move, or overwrite anything in docs/ except when a numbered prompt explicitly adds or updates docs/SPEC.md.

Every screen must work and be checked at 375, 768, 1024 and 1440 px, mobile-first, with the desktop sidebar layout from 1024 px up and reading text limited to about 65 characters per line.

Layout depends only on viewport width (CSS breakpoints, matchMedia). Never use navigator.userAgent, navigator.platform, or other device sniffing. Content uses the shared PageContainer variants.

Every dialog or sheet uses the shared Modal / useModal stack (focus trap, inert background, scroll lock, Escape, focus restore).

Never nest an interactive element inside a link or button.

User content is rendered only as React text nodes, never as HTML strings (no dangerouslySetInnerHTML or innerHTML).

Any feature that stores structured content must have a zod schema, a size limit, and a test that every editor output shape is accepted by that schema.

Final reports must list every requested item as DONE, NOT DONE, or PARTIAL with an honest reason. Do not mark DONE when any part was skipped or only partly implemented.
